Vendored or copied into this repository
---------------------------------------

Durin (https://github.com/ensdomains/durin) — MIT.
  contracts/lib/durin-L1Resolver.deployable.txt is the creation bytecode of
  Durin's L1Resolver with its constructor arguments stripped, so MuseName can
  deploy its own instance. Provenance and the verification steps are in
  contracts/lib/README.md. L2Registry, the registry factory and the signature
  validator used on chain are Durin's own deployments, byte-for-byte.

ERC-8412 draft and its conformance vectors — CC0.
  docs/reference/erc-8412-*.md is the specification text as published in
  ethereum/ERCs#2002, and packages/verify/test/fixtures/erc8412/ holds that
  project's own off-chain test vectors, fetched by
  scripts/fetch-erc8412-vectors.mjs with the commit and per-file hashes recorded
  in the manifest beside them.

forge-std (https://github.com/foundry-rs/forge-std) — MIT, under contracts/lib.

Dependencies (not vendored; installed from npm)
-----------------------------------------------

viem, hono, @hono/node-server, zod, next, react, @modelcontextprotocol/sdk,
@adraffy/ens-normalize, ethers (development only, for compatibility tests),
vitest, typescript, foundry tooling.

Each keeps its own licence, listed in its package metadata.

What this notice is for
-----------------------
So that anyone reading this repository can tell which parts are ours, which are
somebody else's, and on what terms — the same reason the deployment records list
every address and transaction instead of asking for trust.
